{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794757838,"nonce":"7L7nQmFQpmyDLfNQCayRH7PBRgg=","message":"Ash backend in hx-n/hxn-gpu-webgpu 5b09546: lib.rs is the shared API and delegates to src/emscripten.rs (webgpu.h) or src/agent/ (a threaded Ash side module). The agent backend encodes calls onto x-idl's wire (src/agent/wire.rs and page/gpu_webgpu_service.mjs, generated by tools/wire from xgpu's webgpu.idl and canvas.idl, x-idl 753610fd), hands batches to a mailbox in shared memory, and starts the page's agent through ash_host_agent(\"gpu_webgpu\"); page/gpu_webgpu.mjs starts gpu_webgpu_worker.mjs, which serves the mailbox on navigator.gpu. Objects are named by handles the library picks; promises are reply records that a thread of the library waits on (MAILBOX.wait_settled) and settles into hxn futures, so nothing depends on Ash's watch polling. hxn e1a2676 carries the crate's page/ beside the program (build, package, hxn.Bind.lib). The check passes with hxn check hl --wasm --threads --browser (Ash 0.1.18) and cpp --wasm --browser, on this Mac's Metal adapter; CI's Browser workflow runs both on macOS and Linux (SwiftShader). Gaps: validation errors under Ash reach only the agent Worker's console (error scopes would cost two round trips per check); no canvas surface yet; no release (needs an hxn release with e1a2676).","files":null}]}